eed **K** (to make 8-9-10-J-Q) → 4 outs.  \n  - Or **7** (to make 7-8-9-10-J) → 4 outs.  \n  - Total: **8 outs** (~17% chance to hit on river).  \n  - So folding loses equity. Not justified.  \n\nBest Move: Small **raise (100)** to bluff or extract thin value, representing a made hand (like top pair or better), capitalizing on opponent’s passivity.\n\nReason:  \nOpponent has checked through two streets, indicating weakness. You can credibly represent having a queen or a straight (e.g., J-10). A small raise of 100 (minimal investment) can force a fold from marginal hands like middle pair or weak draws. Even if called, you still have outs to win on river. Checking gives up initiative. Raising has positive expected value compared to checking.\n\nAnswer: 100'}
