ive, a small c-bet for value/protection makes sense.\n\nReason:  \nMaking a small bet (e.g., 100) protects your hand by charging draws (like flush draws or gutshots), continues your aggression from pre-flop, and may cause weaker hands (like AQ, KQ, or underpairs) to fold. Going all-in is too strong and likely only gets called by better hands. Folding is irrational with a pair. Checking allows opponents to realize equity cheaply.\n\nThus, a modest bet of 100 is balanced and effective given stack sizes and board dynamics.\n\nAnswer: 100"}
